    "description": "## Source of truth\n\nhttps://jumpr.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/JK/pages/269090817/03+User+Stories+Jira+Disposition\n\n## Outcome\n\nSLC intake captures the stable Affiliate Link identifier supplied by CMS without making link resolution a requirement for accepting the click.\n\n## Requirements\n\n* CMS returns `link_external_id` on the click/SLC request.\n* Store the raw identifier on Study Link Click in a Text field sized for the approved identifier.\n* Preserve the existing permissive landing-zone behavior:\n\n    * blank/unrecognized Link External ID never causes the intake insert to fail;\n    * no lookup/validation is required in the synchronous intake transaction.\n    \n* `link_code` may remain available for diagnostics/human readability but is not the canonical cross-system resolver.\n* Existing response shape remains unchanged unless the external contract requires otherwise.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Valid Link External ID is stored exactly as received.\n2. Blank/unknown value still allows the SLC insert.\n3. Intake does not synchronously require a matching Affiliate Link.\n4. Downstream async processing can use the raw Link External ID for WAGR-50 resolution.\n\n## Dependency\n\nCMS/Strah must add and return `link_external_id`. WAGR-490 defines the Salesforce Link External ID.",
